A class only an XML resource names has to be kept

0018 stopped the crash by not inflating the wrapper when the icon treatment is
off. It did not make the package consistent: res/drawable-v26/
adaptive_icon_drawable_wrapper.xml still names
com.android.launcher3.graphics.FixedScaleDrawable, and the shrinker still
drops that class, because the only Java reference to it is in a branch the
constant-false flag makes dead. The resource and the dex disagree, and anything
that inflates that drawable -- a later change here, or framework code reached
some other way -- takes the launcher down again.

proguard.flags already carries exactly this rule for the sibling class,
ShadowDrawable, for exactly this reason: a drawable that only an XML file names
has no reference a shrinker can see. Upstream got away without the rule for
FixedScaleDrawable only because wrapToAdaptiveIconDrawable() referenced it.
This adds the missing half, which is what AOSP would have had to do had it
shipped the flag off.

diff --git a/proguard.flags b/proguard.flags
index 51abcca..f1f7a35 100644
--- a/proguard.flags
+++ b/proguard.flags
@@ -86,6 +86,17 @@
   public <init>(...);
 }
 
+# PW3: the same reason as the line above, for the sibling class. A drawable
+# that only an XML resource names has no reference the shrinker can see;
+# upstream got away without this one because wrapToAdaptiveIconDrawable()
+# referenced it, and with LEGACY_ICON_TREATMENT off (0017) that method returns
+# before it does. res/drawable-v26/adaptive_icon_drawable_wrapper.xml went on
+# naming the class after the shrinker had dropped it, and the first icon the
+# cache missed took the launcher down at every start.
+-keep class com.android.launcher3.graphics.FixedScaleDrawable {
+  public <init>(...);
+}
+
 # Proguard will strip methods required for talkback to properly scroll to
 # next row when focus is on the last item of last row when using a RecyclerView
 # Keep optimized and shrunk proguard to prevent issues like this when using
